  partName: Fuel Injector 12
  description: The High Pressure Turbine Shaft is a thin, flat, tiny part located
    at the middle-center-center of the engine, constructed from high-pressure shaft
    material. It is vital for transmitting power from the high-pressure turbine to
    the engine's gearbox, driving the engine's accessories. A notable feature of
    this shaft is its ability to withstand extremely high pressures and stresses
    while maintaining rotational stability.
